1
00:00:02,950 --> 00:00:04,971
Get ready for something wild!

2
00:00:04,971 --> 00:00:07,759
The tallest sand dunes in North America.

3
00:00:07,759 --> 00:00:10,617
A waterfall hidden inside a rock crevice.

4
00:00:10,617 --> 00:00:14,520
And a creek that flows like ocean waves across the sand!

5
00:00:15,470 --> 00:00:23,765
This is Great Sand Dunes: 38 miles from Alamosa to the tallest dunes in North America, with a hidden waterfall on the way.

6
00:00:23,765 --> 00:00:27,300
Stick around till the end for the full trip planner!

7
00:00:28,250 --> 00:00:29,359
Here's the plan!

8
00:00:29,359 --> 00:00:37,120
We leave Alamosa, hike to Zapata Falls, stop at the visitor center, and head out onto the dunes at Medano Creek!

9
00:00:38,070 --> 00:00:45,662
We're starting in Alamosa, right in the middle of the San Luis Valley, one of the biggest high mountain valleys in the world!

10
00:00:45,662 --> 00:00:48,760
Grab a sandboard, because we're going to the dunes!

11
00:00:49,710 --> 00:00:54,951
Across the valley floor, with the Sangre de Cristo Mountains straight ahead!

12
00:00:54,951 --> 00:00:59,020
Then a bumpy gravel road takes us up to a hidden waterfall.

13
00:00:59,970 --> 00:01:01,415
This is Zapata Falls!

14
00:01:01,415 --> 00:01:08,090
It's a short hike, then you wade into a crack in the rock, and there's a waterfall hiding inside!

15
00:01:08,090 --> 00:01:10,980
In winter it freezes into a column of ice!

16
00:01:11,930 --> 00:01:16,243
And here come the dunes, piled up right against the mountains!

17
00:01:16,243 --> 00:01:21,530
The winds blow sand across the valley, and the mountains trap it right here.

18
00:01:22,480 --> 00:01:26,915
Here's the visitor center, with the whole dunefield right behind it!

19
00:01:26,915 --> 00:01:30,045
Grab a map, and ask a ranger about Medano Creek.

20
00:01:30,045 --> 00:01:31,610
Then let's hit the sand!

21
00:01:32,560 --> 00:01:35,289
Just down the road to the dunes parking lot.

22
00:01:35,289 --> 00:01:36,530
Shoes off, let's go!

23
00:01:37,480 --> 00:01:41,032
This is it, the tallest sand dunes in North America!

24
00:01:41,032 --> 00:01:44,243
Star Dune rises about seven hundred fifty feet.

25
00:01:44,243 --> 00:01:51,620
And in late spring, Medano Creek flows right across the sand in little waves, like a beach in the mountains!

26
00:01:52,570 --> 00:01:54,323
And that's the drive!

27
00:01:54,323 --> 00:01:59,750
38 miles from Alamosa to the tallest sand dunes in North America.

28
00:02:00,700 --> 00:02:03,860
Here's your trip planner, everything in one place.

29
00:02:03,860 --> 00:02:05,630
Pause and grab a screenshot!

30
00:02:09,200 --> 00:02:10,870
Thanks for riding along!

31
00:02:10,870 --> 00:02:17,200
Hit subscribe, and next time we're driving from Colorado Springs to the Royal Gorge Bridge!
